Here is an example of a JavaScript program that reads a text file line by line and counts the number of occurrences of a specific word in the file:

```
// File reader object
const fs = require('fs');

// Specify the file path
const filePath = 'example.txt';

// Read the file line by line
fs.readFile(filePath, 'line', (err, data) => {
  if (err) throw err;

  // Split the data into lines
  const lines = data.toString().split('\n');

  // Specify the word to search for
  const searchWord = 'example';

  // Initialize a counter to keep track of the number of occurrences of the word
  let count = 0;

  // Iterate over the lines
  for (const line of lines) {
    // Check if the line contains the word
    if (line.includes(searchWord)) {
      // Increment the counter if it does
      count++;
    }
  }

  // Print the result
  console.log(`Number of occurrences of ${searchWord} in the file: ${count}`);
});
```

This program uses the Node.js `fs` module to read the file, and the `includes()` method to check if a line contains the specified word. The program will search for the word `example` in the file `example.txt` and will print the number of occurrences of the word in the file.
